Description:

A Sieve fileinto that targets a mailbox the script owner doesn't own, by name
or by :mailboxid, now requires the "i" (insert) right on it.  Previously "p"
(post) was enough, so a mailbox granting "anyone p" for plus-addressing
could be filed into from any other user's script, bypassing its owner's
own Sieve script.  A Sieve mailboxid, as used by :mailboxid and
mailboxidexists, now matches another user's mailbox only if the script
owner has "l" (lookup) on it.


Documentation:

None


Config changes:

